From: huhucapture contributors <huhucapture@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Renew the backend copy session before a consumer resumes

Project-local correction against Portal-wlr 0.8.1 plus patches 0001-0006.
The locked ext-image-copy-capture protocol permits an indefinite wait on
unchanged content after a session's first successful frame. A new PipeWire
consumer therefore needs a fresh backend copy session of the same target.
The Portal authorization, selected source and PipeWire node remain alive.

Close the copy session on STREAMING-to-PAUSED even without a held buffer.
Before dequeue, create the replacement session and wait for its asynchronous
initial constraints.done. Only then resume the existing producer graph.
Cancel the old frame/FPS work and clear partial constraints on close; retain
the current negotiated constraints for the existing PipeWire node. Release
the temporary source proxy after the new session retains the source.

This introduces no synthetic damage, replacement pixels, first-frame drop,
new authorization, relaxed deadline or changed native acceptance assertion.
License: MIT, as the unchanged upstream LICENSE and this project.

Protocol: wayland-protocols 1.41, 71da8bd7f9fd3ea7c5d87ad19ca087eeca137673
